
==============================================================================
1. J = I(X_0) cap I(N) is radical -- both factors are prime
==============================================================================
  I(X_0(m003)) quotient ~= Q[x,x^-1]        : domain -> prime
  I(X_0(m006)) quotient ~= Q[x,(x-1)^-1,(x+1)^-1] : domain -> prime
  I(N) = <x-z,y-2> quotient ~= Q[t] (t=x=z)  : domain -> prime
  N != X_0 in either case (line vs curve of different type)
  => I(X_0) cap I(N) is an intersection of two DISTINCT PRIME
     ideals, hence automatically RADICAL (sqrt(P cap Q) = P cap Q
     whenever P,Q are already radical). No further computation
     changes this conclusion.

==============================================================================
2a. every KNOWN genuine collision (both manifolds) vanishes on N
==============================================================================
  m003: 21 genuine deltas; m006: 26 genuine deltas; union: 46 distinct polynomials
  vanish identically on N (no manifold relation imposed): 46/46
  => N is proved ambient directly, for every known genuine collision,
     WITHOUT needing to test a third manifold's relator.

==============================================================================
2b. this is not trivial -- only ~21% of ALL word-pairs vanish on N
==============================================================================
  total word pairs in the 99-word universe: 4851 (= C(99,2))
  pairs whose trace difference vanishes ambiently on N: 1028 (21.2%)
  => the 'N-vanishing set' is a genuine, nontrivial, well-defined
     combinatorial subset of the atlas -- not a universal identity
     -- and both manifolds' entire genuine-collision sets are
     contained in it.

==============================================================================
3. consequence: a component-generating pair CANNOT exist within length <=6
==============================================================================
  Since every genuine bounded-length (<=6) atlas collision difference
  lies in I(N) (part 2a), any ideal generated by a finite subset of
  them is contained in I(X_0) cap I(N), which is a PROPER sub-ideal
  of I(X_0) (verified exactly in
  m003_m006_atlas_ideal_vs_component_ideal.py). Therefore NO finite
  collection of atlas collisions (word length <=6) can generate the
  full component ideal I(X_0) for either manifold -- this rules out,
  by necessity rather than absence of search, the proposed 'minimal
  pair (Delta_1,Delta_2) with <Delta_1,Delta_2>=P_006' construction
  within this word-length bound. A genuinely component-generating
  pair, if one exists, requires words of length > 6 (untested here).

